  "articleBody": "Installing a Lazy Susan can significantly improve your kitchen's organization, but sometimes the DIY path hits a snag. Knowing when to call in a professional can save you a lot of headache and potential damage. Here are some key indicators: \n\n*   **Irregular Corner Cabinets:** If your corner cabinet isn't a standard size or shape, getting a pre-made Lazy Susan to fit perfectly can be a real challenge. \n*   **Uneven Surfaces:** If your cabinet box or the floor within the cabinet is out of level, it can cause the Lazy Susan to rub, wobble, or bind during rotation. A professional can correct these issues. \n*   **Custom Fitting Needed:** Sometimes, a Lazy Susan unit needs trimming or custom adjustments to fit snugly and operate smoothly, which requires specific tools and expertise. \n*   **Obstructions:** If you have existing plumbing, wiring, or other fixed obstructions inside the cabinet that the Lazy Susan needs to work around, a pro can navigate these complexities safely. \n\nFor these trickier installations, HH Remodeling LLC is here to help homeowners throughout the greater Denver area. We'll ensure your Lazy Susan is installed perfectly, so it turns smoothly and silently every time.",
  "datePublished": "2026-08-09"
